Subject: [PATCH 3/3] claude/skills: Thread each revision under its first
 version
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: rkrlzwxwostolzxrwwzpsqlpnklxmsns
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 05:26:09 +0000

patch-triage grouped resends on the assumption that each is a thread
of its own, and would read one thread holding v1 through v3 as a
single entry without knowing why. It now expects versions in one
thread, with older resends still apart.

freebsd-port formats with plain git format-patch in a ports tree, so
format-patch.sh never picks the reply target there. It now says to
pass --in-reply-to with v1, so ports revisions thread like the rest.
